WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:07.839
“Please, good sir, I beseech you, as a man
of science, nay, as a man of reason, you mustn’t

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:11.559
stifle my research at this critical juncture!

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:18.010
You have no idea how close I am to finding
a cure for this blasted Pestilence.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:23.430
I need only a handful of live subjects to
complete my research...”

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:28.530
The Plague Doctor’s emphatic pleas fell
on deaf ears, as a stone-faced researcher

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.390
took notes on his latest pontifications.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:38.489
The Doctor - whom those clods had reduced
so rudely to a mere number, SCP-049 - banged

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:40.760
his gloved fist up against the wall.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:46.269
And to think, he once thought of these men
as intellectual equals - Fellow travelers

00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:49.519
on the road to scientific enlightenment!

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:52.179
What a positively sick joke...

00:00:52.179 --> 00:00:56.570
Before the Doctor got another chance to appeal
for his right to experiment, the researcher

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.449
left him alone once more.

00:00:58.449 --> 00:01:01.269
A truly sad state of affairs.

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:03.989
Nobody appreciated a true scientist in this
day and age.

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:10.490
It was sure to be another day of languishing
alone in his cell, wishing he had the capacity

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.780
to do more.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.950
So he was as surprised as anyone when alarms
started going off, and the door of his cell

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.280
swung open, automatically.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.480
The Plague Doctor stepped out of the cell
and into the hall, where many other humanoid

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.450
anomalies were roaming, confused as to why
they’d been suddenly released.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:28.810
What was happening?

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:33.420
As it turned out, what was happening was one
of the most brutal Chaos Insurgency raids

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.200
the staff of Site-19 had ever seen.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.460
It had been planned immaculately.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:43.920
You see, guards rotate semi-regularly at Site-19
due to the high-pressure nature of the job.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.780
Lots of deaths and mental breakdowns, as you
probably correctly predicted.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:54.590
Even the administrative staff of the SCP Foundation
are only human - Well, mostly, anyway - So

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.270
they’re not immune to little oversights
here and there.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:02.250
And it’s in those oversights that expertly
trained Chaos Insurgency Infiltration Agents

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.500
make their living.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:09.159
No less than fifteen of them had been working
undercover in Site-19 for just over two weeks,

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:16.569
and they did a fine job of lowering the metaphorical
drawbridge for a heavily armed invasion force.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:20.310
The guards who weren’t plants were quickly
murdered by the infiltrators, and even some

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:25.280
of the on-site Task Forces were quickly overwhelmed
and gunned down by the high-precision rifles

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.209
of the Chaos Insurgency’s finest.

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:31.569
While the front liners were distracted by
the sudden assault, the infiltrators found

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:36.969
their way to the site’s security control
room and massacred everyone inside.

00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:42.040
Opening every single door in the site was
as simple as putting in a few stolen key codes

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.079
and flipping a few carefully-remembered switches.

00:02:45.079 --> 00:02:50.129
Consequently, while Foundation Agents and
Chaos Insurgency mercenaries clashed sabers,

00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:55.580
high-priority anomalies like SCP-049 simply
wandered the facility, watching the calamity

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.430
unfold from within.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:03.269
The Foundation was beset on all sides: Shot
at by heavily-armed maniacs and attacked from

00:03:03.269 --> 00:03:09.029
within by the numerous roaming anomalous entities
that were eager to get their hands on Foundation

00:03:09.029 --> 00:03:10.359
personnel.

00:03:10.359 --> 00:03:13.359
Definitely not an ideal situation, to say
the least.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:19.310
The Plague Doctor only had one thing on his
mind, though: “Hmmm, this definitely won’t

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.189
do my research any good.

00:03:21.189 --> 00:03:25.569
Unless I can escape and find my way to a suitable
laboratory.

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:28.769
Oh, now there’s an idea...”

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:33.439
But his scientific fantasies were soon interrupted
by a Chaos Insurgency soldier swinging the

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:39.889
butt of his M4 Carbine into his avian exo-skull
with a supremely unpleasant crack.

00:03:39.889 --> 00:03:45.069
The Doctor was dazed by it momentarily, the
pain coming at him like a thunderclap, but

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:48.959
the Insurgent never got the chance to take
another swing.

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:53.599
Before the Insurgent could do anything, the
Plague Doctor lunged out with practiced speed,

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.420
grasping him by the throat.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.419
Immediately, everything went black, and the
Insurgent’s limp corpse collapsed to the

00:03:59.419 --> 00:04:00.419
ground.

00:04:00.419 --> 00:04:05.500
Serves him right, the Doctor internally mused,
soldiers attacking medics is violating even

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.099
the most basic rules of gentlemanly warfare!

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:12.760
Then, another flash of immense pain, as a
different rifle butt collided with the back

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:13.810
of his head.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:18.549
The Doctor fell to one knee, feeling dizzy,
but before he could retaliate, he felt the

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:22.599
two sharp prongs of a cattle prod pressing
up against his neck.

00:04:22.599 --> 00:04:26.940
The sudden rush of electricity surged through
his neck, sending his muscles into a wave

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.110
of involuntary spasms.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:34.020
The Insurgents crowding around him chimed
in with their own agonizing cattle prods,

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:38.660
relentlessly shocking him until the flashes
of white-hot pain soon became an oppressive

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.509
blanket of total dark.

00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:46.110
Even on his most cantankerous days, the SCP
Foundation had never treated him like this...

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:51.280
When he eventually came to, he was still in
darkness, standing upright, with high-tech

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.940
shackles holding every limb in place.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.990
It was beyond uncomfortable for the poor Plague
Doctor, but it succeeded in the task of keeping

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.530
him under control.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.150
He couldn’t move an inch.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:07.289
There were muffled voices beyond the dark,
beyond the confines of this new containment.

00:05:07.289 --> 00:05:11.729
The modulated gas-mask voices of Insurgents,
and something else.

00:05:11.729 --> 00:05:16.169
Faintly accented, oddly familiar, but he couldn’t
quite place it.

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:21.039
Soon, the voices were replaced by another
sound: The grinding of crowbars levering nails

00:05:21.039 --> 00:05:22.610
out of cheap wood.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:27.180
With a creaking tumble, a rectangle of bright
light opened up in front of him, populated

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.139
by a number of silhouettes.

00:05:29.139 --> 00:05:34.319
On either side were Chaos Insurgents in familiar
tactical garb, and in between them stood a

00:05:34.319 --> 00:05:40.139
tall, well-groomed man with an expensive-looking
purple smoking jacket and a pencil mustache.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:45.110
For the first few fractions of a second, his
face was a portrait of excitement.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.259
But as he took in the sight of the Plague
Doctor standing before him, all the joy drained

00:05:49.259 --> 00:05:50.800
from his snooty countenance.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.949
“What the hell am I looking at here?”

00:05:52.949 --> 00:05:54.770
the man in the smoking jacket said.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:59.370
The Doctor, indignant at such a response from
the man who’d presumably ordered his assault,

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.919
rasped, “A man of science, good sir.”

00:06:02.919 --> 00:06:07.580
The man in the smoking jacket ignored him
and continued to berate the Chaos Insurgents,

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:12.380
with an odd level of confidence for someone
reprimanding trained, cold-blooded killers.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:18.099
“I wanted SCP-650, the Startling Statue,
not this clownish Ren Faire cosplayer!

00:06:18.099 --> 00:06:20.110
What the hell did I pay you ruffians for?

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:25.110
I was told you ‘Chaos Insurgents’ were
the very best at this, and for your hefty

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.599
price, I expect excellence!”

00:06:27.599 --> 00:06:32.010
The rant continued much like this, leaving
everyone in attendance - the Insurgents, the

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:36.909
Plague Doctor - feeling thoroughly exhausted
by him and unable to do anything about it.

00:06:36.909 --> 00:06:42.610
You see, this wasn’t just any Chaos Insurgency
client - Your average tinpot dictator or arms

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.470
dealer, you know the type.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:51.120
This was the one and only Pascal Laget: One
of the most famous, or rather, infamous, Anart

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.819
Collectors in the game.

00:06:52.819 --> 00:06:56.939
He’d been a Foundation Person of Interest
for years due to his dealings with the Chaos

00:06:56.939 --> 00:07:01.360
Insurgency and Marshall, Carter, and Dark
Ltd., all to the end of expanding his Anart

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:06.750
Collection, but his vast wealth and connections
had always shielded him from Foundation probes.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.590
For those unfamiliar with the subculture,
Anart - short for Anomalous Art - is exactly

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:16.419
what it sounds like: Artistic projects with
anomalous properties to give it that extra

00:07:16.419 --> 00:07:17.419
kick.

00:07:17.419 --> 00:07:21.659
One of the most popular Groups of Interest
dealing in Anart is the iconic Are We Cool

00:07:21.659 --> 00:07:27.949
Yet?, which, incidentally, had recently excommunicated
Pascal Laget for being an exceedingly wealthy,

00:07:27.949 --> 00:07:32.340
up-tight Square who really didn’t represent
the collective’s rebellious ethos.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:37.000
And considering his response was to pay the
Chaos Insurgency to Raid Site-19 for a few

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.689
pieces for his own private collection, costing
him millions of dollars and both groups many

00:07:41.689 --> 00:07:44.900
lives, it was safe to say he wasn’t taking
it well.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.949
“Look, we got you that other statue and
that thing killed four of our best guys, so

00:07:48.949 --> 00:07:52.040
how about we just call it even?” said one
of the Insurgents.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:55.020
“I’m sure you can have fun with bird-brain
here, too.”

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.440
Pascal tutted and reluctantly dismissed his
hired guns.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:03.100
Having the Plague Doctor here definitely wasn’t
ideal, especially considering he wanted to

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:07.550
host the ultimate Anart exhibition to put
Are We Cool Yet’s worthless Sommes-Nous

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.030
Devenus Magnifiques?

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:12.590
to shame, but he would make do with what he
had.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:17.289
Perhaps he could say that 049 was a commentary
on the ever-present nature of disease in mankind’s

00:08:17.289 --> 00:08:20.199
life, and our forever archaic approach to
it.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:22.719
Yes, yes, that would do nicely...

00:08:22.719 --> 00:08:28.159
Needless to say, the Plague Doctor was infuriated
by all of this: The violence against his person,

00:08:28.159 --> 00:08:33.260
the kidnapping, the disrespect, and most of
all, the interruption to his precious research

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:37.729
- especially considering how close he’d
gotten to finding a cure for the Pestilence!

00:08:37.729 --> 00:08:42.700
But instead, he was soon spirited by a legion
of heavily-armored goons from his wooden box

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:46.290
to a glass one in one of Laget’s many opulent
hallways.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:50.860
There were other glass cases on either side
of him, and more on the other side of the

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:51.860
hall.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:56.070
All too reinforced for the Plague Doctor to
ever smash through on his own.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.070
Damn it.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:09:02.060
Laget’s own private Anart exhibition, probably
wedged between his oversized dining room and

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.850
his jewel-encrusted crapper.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.630
Occasionally, Pascal himself would jaunt down
the hallway to gaze upon his new stolen Anart

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:12.290
pieces, and of course, the Plague Doctor would
try his best to reason with him.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:17.540
“I am a patient man, Monsieur Laget, but
this is simply barbaric!

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:20.280
By what right do you imprison me here?

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.890
Is your intention to deprive the world, the
entire human race, of my valuable medical

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:26.120
breakthroughs?

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.710
Could you live with that on your conscience,
good sir?”

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.950
There was never any meaningful response.

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:36.139
The Plague Doctor soon learned that Pascal
Laget didn’t like his art interactive.

00:09:36.139 --> 00:09:41.380
It was simply meant to languish away in a
glass box, being watched, being passively

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:42.470
looked at.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:46.560
Those Chaos Insurgency louts hadn’t even
bothered to bring his notebook or medical

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.750
bag, so he was without the tools to even perform
his experiments.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:55.860
As loathed as he was to admit it, this was
even worse than being locked up by the SCP

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:56.860
Foundation.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.290
But all of this wasn’t entirely unfamiliar.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:04.360
There was something in the glass box across
from the Plague Doctor that he vaguely recognized

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:05.360
back from Site-19.

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:10.860
He’d never seen it up close, but he’d
heard researchers speaking about it, and even

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:12.760
seen a few pictures.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:16.279
And such a strange construction it was...

00:10:16.279 --> 00:10:21.420
A peculiar, haphazard Sculpture made from
concrete, rebar, and spray paint.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:26.880
Quite ugly, in this humble Doctor’s opinion,
but there was something oddly entrancing about

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:27.880
it.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:31.620
And for reasons beyond the Doctor’s recollection,
four of Laget’s men stood around the glass

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:35.610
box it was being stored in, always watching.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:40.279
The men were frequently switched in and out,
as though they were watching it in shifts,

00:10:40.279 --> 00:10:44.440
always fixing their gaze on its peculiar,
malformed body.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.621
Maybe it was all the electric shocks and knocks
to the head, but he just couldn’t remember

00:10:48.621 --> 00:10:52.310
why Pascal was having the piece so carefully
observed.

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:57.199
But he knew, on some primal level, that the
secret to this would perhaps be the key to

00:10:57.199 --> 00:10:58.390
his own escape.

00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:59.800
If only he could remember...

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:04.920
Still, time passed, Pascal drifted in and
out, sometimes with guests.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.839
The Plague Doctor had learned not to speak.

00:11:07.839 --> 00:11:10.139
These animals could not be reasoned with.

00:11:10.139 --> 00:11:15.579
As a scientist, he would instead carefully
observe, until his observations bore fruit.

00:11:15.579 --> 00:11:20.430
He noticed that Pascal’s guests - All people
who looked equally as wealthy and pompous

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:26.600
as Pascal himself - all seemed to look right
over him, and instead focus on the ugly statue

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:32.279
across the hall, still forever observed by
any four of Pascal’s men.

00:11:32.279 --> 00:11:35.670
Some of them looked actively nervous, just
being in its presence.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:36.670
Curious.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.760
The Plague Doctor made a mental note of this.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:42.870
Just as he did when Pascal gave his guests
a reassuring pat on the shoulder, and told

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.510
them, “Please, calm yourself.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:48.330
It’s harmless while my personnel are keeping
an eye on it.”

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:53.120
Little by little, the Plague Doctor’s memories
of his infamous neighbor had begun to return.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:59.200
He knew what he must do to escape, now all
he needed to do was wait for the perfect moment.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:03.430
Soon enough, Pascal’s mansion was filled
with a bevy of Anart snobs from hither and

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:04.430
yarn.

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:07.380
A private soirée, to show off his new collection.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:13.070
They wandered the halls in three-piece tuxedos
and designer ballroom dresses, sipping champagne

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:15.020
from imported crystal.

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:20.459
All such lovely, refined, high society people,
and if the good Doctor’s plan went off as

00:12:20.459 --> 00:12:26.500
he intended, they would all be such lovely,
refined, high society corpses.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:30.920
The Plague Doctor waited until, mercifully,
he and the four members of personnel watching

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.259
the Sculpture were the only ones left in the
hallway.

00:12:33.259 --> 00:12:38.610
He’d been so good, so patient, that none
of the men guarding the Sculpture at present

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.990
had ever heard him make a noise.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:45.399
He was so invisible to them that, in all likelihood,
they probably didn’t even notice he could

00:12:45.399 --> 00:12:46.630
make a sound.

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:50.370
And that worked for his purposes just fine.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:55.480
Though in any case, if he wanted this to work,
he would need to time his plan perfectly.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:59.680
Even a fraction of a second out of place,
and the whole thing would have dire consequences.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:04.389
Still, the Doctor was still a Frenchman at
heart, and as a Frenchman, he knew he would

00:13:04.389 --> 00:13:09.660
rather die nobly in the process of escape
than remain captured by this worthless buffoon.

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:15.000
He’d be sure to take as many of these men
down with him in the process as he was able.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:19.620
The Plague Doctor exhaled deeply, drawing
a lungful of air, then bellowed as loud as

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.160
he possibly could.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:26.190
The sudden, unexpected noise was so shocking
that it jogged the four watchers almost reflexively

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:28.030
to turn and look at him.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:32.380
And in that split second that they did, the
Plague Doctor closed his eyes.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:38.339
In the dark, time seemed to move slower - Perhaps
due to the Doctor’s keen focus, cultivated

00:13:38.339 --> 00:13:40.010
over many a century.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:46.380
He listened carefully to the sequence of sounds:
Glass shattering, four choked gasps in sequence,

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:51.170
four brutal crunches, then, nanoseconds later,
more glass shattering—

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:54.480
The Plague Doctor’s eyes snapped open, just
in time.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:59.980
Just as predicted, the Sculpture, being entirely
unobserved, had smashed through its glass

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:04.620
case, murdered all four members of personnel
by snapping their necks, and then smashed

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:07.720
through his own glass case to do the same
to him.

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:11.550
The Plague Doctor had cut it so close, in
fact, that he opened his eyes to the face

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:16.970
of the Sculpture staring into his own, its
concrete limbs wrapped around his neck.

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:19.060
Very good timing, indeed.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:22.980
With a sigh of relief, the Plague Doctor slipped
out of the Sculpture’s concrete grasp, and

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:27.790
backed down the hallway, keeping his gaze
fixed on the Sculpture the entire time.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:32.899
He’d heard it decimate Pascal’s men, he
certainly didn’t fancy undergoing the same

00:14:32.899 --> 00:14:33.899
fate.

00:14:33.899 --> 00:14:37.259
The second the Plague Doctor backed around
the corner, rendering the Sculpture - or as

00:14:37.259 --> 00:14:42.670
the SCP Foundation called it, SCP-173 - out
of sight, he could hear terrified screaming

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:45.029
coming from the other end of the hall.

00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:49.620
He was not a sadistic man, but the Plague
Doctor would be lying if he told you he didn’t

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:53.660
take just a little bit of pleasure in hearing
that sound.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.519
Somewhere else in the vast mansion of Pascal
Laget, the Sculpture was slaughtering its

00:14:57.519 --> 00:15:02.600
way through servants and party guests, while
the Plague Doctor searched for some kind of

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:03.600
exit.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:07.420
Anyone who dared get in his way was given
a swift and merciless touch of death, sending

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:10.519
their body unceremoniously to the ground.

00:15:10.519 --> 00:15:15.240
Anyone in his way was preventing him from
finding a cure for the Pestilence, and thus,

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:17.279
endangering countless lives.

00:15:17.279 --> 00:15:22.279
It was, of course, regrettable to have to
kill anyone, but some sacrifices must be made

00:15:22.279 --> 00:15:23.850
for the greater good of mankind.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:24.850
Well...

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:28.389
It’s not necessarily ‘always’ regrettable,
per se.

00:15:28.389 --> 00:15:33.440
On his way out, while the murderous rampage
of SCP-173 seemed to distract anyone of note,

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:38.660
the Plague Doctor just so happened to encounter
a fleeing Pascal Laget, hoping to find some

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:40.690
kind of escape himself.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.779
It seemed that, now, fate was on his side
once more.

00:15:43.779 --> 00:15:49.230
To have his jailor right here, in the palm
of his hand, would be such a perfect parting

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.230
gift...

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:53.000
Funnily enough, Pascal was far more talkative
to him now.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.800
He rattled off a rapid-fire series of threats,
bribes, and pleas, claiming in the end that

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:59.560
he never meant any harm.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.160
He was the one who freed the Plague Doctor
from the SCP Foundation.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.350
They were on the same side here.

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:07.180
All this was for the art.

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:09.180
No offense was ever intended.

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:12.750
Pascal Laget simply lived for art.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:19.660
“Then die for it, good sir,” the Plague
Doctor said, and with a single touch, Pascal’s

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:24.230
eyes rolled up into the back of his head,
and he fell to the ground, dead.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:29.339
It was one of the few non-scientific deaths
that he felt truly no guilt for.

00:16:29.339 --> 00:16:33.449
After some time searching, the screams around
the rest of the mansion eventually went silent.

00:16:33.449 --> 00:16:35.709
That did wonders for his focus.

00:16:35.709 --> 00:16:40.100
It didn’t take long for the Plague Doctor
to locate an exit - A fine, mahogany door

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:45.699
with elaborate adornments befitting a man
as gaudy as Pascal - and begin strolling towards

00:16:45.699 --> 00:16:48.650
it, his chest swollen with pride and a sense
of accomplishment.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:53.130
Then he blinked, and a few feet in front of
him stood The Sculpture.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:57.649
It was there so suddenly that the Plague Doctor
fell backwards in shock, but he devoted everything

00:16:57.649 --> 00:16:59.870
to keeping an eye on that monstrosity.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:04.510
With everyone else in the mansion presumably
dead at this point, it had now come back for

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:05.510
him.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:10.370
It stood there, staring, silently, ready to
exact the terrible price for freeing it as

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.880
soon as the doctor dared to blink.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:17.000
The Plague Doctor began crawling backwards
down the hall, just wanting to put some distance

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.110
between himself and the Sculpture.

00:17:19.110 --> 00:17:23.339
As the seconds passed, he could feel his eyes
drying out, until the inevitable...

00:17:23.339 --> 00:17:24.589
Blink.

00:17:24.589 --> 00:17:28.830
The Sculpture was standing right in front
of him now, gazing down, almost mocking.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:30.870
It had closed the distance so quickly.

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:35.390
If the Plague Doctor blinked again, he was
sure that his eyes would never open again.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:40.500
All it had to do was wait as the seconds passed,
and the Doctor began to feel his eyes drying

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.600
up again.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:46.539
That subtle sting quickly grew into a nagging
pain that could not be denied.

00:17:46.539 --> 00:17:49.500
Sooner or later, he was going to have to...

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.500
BANG!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:54.490
The front door flew open, and in an instant,
the hallway was filled with heavily-armed

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:55.490
troops.

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:59.250
All wearing the familiar black and grey of
the SCP Foundation.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:02.789
The Plague Doctor had never been so relieved
to see the organization that had kept him

00:18:02.789 --> 00:18:04.700
locked up for so many decades.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:08.620
For once, they’d saved him from something
even worse.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:12.549
Of course, the Sculpture didn’t say anything,
but the disappointment of losing that one

00:18:12.549 --> 00:18:17.220
more victim seemed to radiate off of it like
a lingering bad smell.

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:21.309
The Plague Doctor willingly gave himself up,
and heavy machinery was brought in to pick

00:18:21.309 --> 00:18:26.860
up SCP-173 - with the help of the Eye-pods
to make sure it didn’t try any funny business

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:27.860
in transit.

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:32.440
Pascal had gotten away with his shady dealings
for years, but the brazen attack he funded

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:35.789
against Site-19 was now enough for the Foundation
to track him down.

00:18:35.789 --> 00:18:40.450
When his corpse was found in the halls of
his own home, with no obvious cause of death,

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:43.880
we can happily tell you that nobody was disappointed.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:47.260
By the evening, the Plague Doctor was happy
to be back in his cell.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:52.450
His research could continue here, and in time,
he knew that the personnel of the SCP Foundation

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:55.559
would listen to reason and comply with his
demands.

00:18:55.559 --> 00:19:00.820
After all, science marches on, regardless
of who chooses to march with it.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:06.220
But he would forever feel a little nervous
in Site-19 after that, knowing the concrete

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.860
monster he was sharing the building with.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:13.040
He hoped that if ever there was another containment
breach involving that...

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:18.290
Thing, that it didn’t feel like paying him
a visit, for old times’ sake...

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:24.500
Now go check out “SCP-049 The Plague Doctor
- Everything You Need to Know” and “SCP-173

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:28.919
Origin Story - How 173 Got to Site-19” for
more on the two SCPs from today’s original

00:19:28.919 --> 00:19:29.039
tale!

